r `dangling`. Any `dangling` link (or an `@evidence[[...]]` token with no `scientific-evidence/` bundle present) is a hard error and must be sent back to the paper-writing agent for repair.\n3. Validate figure manifest and figure readability budget when `figure_manifest.json` is present or `paper_strategy.json` requires figures. The canonical schema is `templates/figure_manifest.schema.json`.\n```bash\npython .claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py \\\n  --paper-dir .\n```\n4. Compile:\n```bash\nbash scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n```\nThe compile script also validates that Supplementary Information is visibly rendered on a page\nafter References with substantive content. Source-only structure checks are not sufficient for\nconditional or literal LaTeX constructs.\nIt records and validates every LaTeX input, restricts BibTeX to the canonical `references.bib`,\nand removes inherited Kpathsea path overrides before compiling.\n5. Require `paper.pdf` to exist.\n6. When `paper_data.json.paper_profile == \"standalone\"`, also fail on visible paper language that leaks pipeline terms such as `eligible`, `correct and eligible`, `correctness rate`, `worker_01`, `worker_02`, `combined_score`, or similar internal wording.\n7. When the selected format or venue guidance requires real author metadata, also fail on anonymous or generic placeholder author blocks and emit soft warnings when title/abstract/introduction/conclusion lack venue-relevant framing or when the discussion drifts into unrelated application narratives.\n8. Fail hard on any missing grounding link, missing section, missing/empty/misordered Supplementary Information, unresolved citation, bibliography/provenance mismatch, figure-manifest mismatch, density-budget violation, page-limit violation for formats with enforced budgets, standalone-language violation, author-block violation required by format/venue guidance, dangling `@evidence[[...]]` link, or compile error.\n9. Treat the parent orchestrator's validation report as authoritative during repair rounds. Last-body-page fill is rendered geometric vertical occupancy computed from text and graphics bounds, not character count or word density. Do not claim that page validation passed using a character-count proxy. If the canonical validator is unavailable in the agent workspace, make the targeted repair and return control so the parent can compile and revalidate it.\n\n--- MEMORY ---\n---\nname: memory-log\ndescription: Maintain a continuous, append-only `./memory.md` log of discoveries, evaluations, failures, and next hypotheses during agent runs.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nKeep durable run memory so idea evolution and program evidence are never lost between steps.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- At run start to initialize memory.\n- After every meaningful step (`idea`, `edit`, `evaluate`, `verify`, `paper`, `draft`).\n- Immediately after every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair.\n\n# What to do\n1. Initialize `./memory.md` if missing with these section headers:\n- `# Memory Log`\n- `## Context`\n- `## Idea Discoveries`\n- `## Program Evaluations`\n- `## Failures / Regressions`\n- `## Next Hypotheses`\n2. Also initialize global files if missing:\n- `./global_memory/memory.md`\n- `./global_memory/memory.jsonl`\n3. Never delete or rewrite prior entries; append only.\n4. For each appended entry, include:\n- timestamp\n- step type\n- change/discovery summary\n- concrete evidence\n- next action\n5. After every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair, append a `Program Evaluations` entry that includes:\n- `program_<idx>`\n- `combined_score`\n- `correct`\n- rubric pass/fail summary\n- `next_recommendation`\n6. For regressions or failed rubrics, append one root-cause hypothesis under `Failures / Regressions`.\n7. Before exit, append final status (`rubric_pass`, `cap_reached`, or task-specific stop reason) and next hypothesis under `Next Hypotheses`.\n8. When command execution is unavailable, use read/edit/write tools to append directly\nto the required markdown and JSONL files. Preserve all existing content. When command\nexecution is available, prefer the helper for deterministic dual-write:\n- script: detect the active agent config directory first, then use `<that-dir>/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py`\n- command template:\n```bash\nMEMORY_HELPER=\"$(find ./.claude ./.codex ./.cursor ./.opencode ./.gemini ./.pi -path '*/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py' -print -quit 2>/dev/null)\"\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" \\\n  --global-memory-md \"./global_memory/memory.md\" \\\n  --global-memory-jsonl \"./global_memory/memory.jsonl\" \\\n  --event-json '{\"step\":\"evaluate\",\"scope\":\"attempt\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"evidence\":\"...\",\"next_action\":\"...\",\"attempt_id\":\"{{ATTEMPT_ID}}\",\"idea_id\":\"{{IDEA_ID}}\",\"program_id\":\"program_2\",\"metrics\":{\"combined_score\":2.54,\"correct\":true}}'\n```\n9. JSONL event schema (required keys):\n- `timestamp` (auto-filled if omitted)\n- `step` (`idea|edit|evaluate|verify|paper|draft|final|conclusions_skip`)\n- `scope` (`idea|attempt|paper|campaign`)\n- `summary`\n- `evidence`\n- `next_action`\n- optional: `idea_id`, `attempt_id`, `program_id`, `metrics`, `rubrics`, `tags`\n\n10. Update distilled conclusions (`conclusions.md`).\n**Purpose.** `conclusions.md` is a *forward-looking guide* for the next worker (or your future self in a later cycle). Its job is to help readers (a) focus their effort on directions you've found promising, and (b) avoid spending compute on directions you've already shown to be unpromising. Each sentence should either point at a lead worth pursuing or warn against a dead end, framed so a researcher who has not read your `memory.md` can still act on it. Avoid chronology, restate-of-results, and post-mortem narration — those belong in `memory.md`. Conclusions are the synthesis layer that makes other workers' next cycles more efficient.\n\n**When.** After every memory-append in the cycle (idea / edit / evaluate / verify / paper / final), evaluate whether `conclusions.md` should be updated.\n\n**Update gate (the only valid triggers).**\n- (a) cycle **contradicts** an existing sentence → rewrite that sentence.\n- (b) cycle opens a **new category** not yet covered → add a sentence.\n- (c) cycle **flips a Do/Don't** recommendation → flip it.\n- (d) cycle **meaningfully refines** an existing sentence — narrows the conditions under which a rule holds, broadens its applicability to a config it wasn't known to apply to, sharpens a tentative claim into a confident one, or adds a qualifier the prior phrasing didn't cover → edit the sentence to incorporate the refinement. Simple re-confirmation in the same regime is **not** sufficient; you must identify the refinement dimension (narrow / broaden / sharpen / qualify) in `--gate-reason`.\n- otherwise → **keep**, do not invoke the helper.\n\n**Format constraints.** Single paragraph. ≤300 words. No blank lines (`\\n\\n`). Avoid detailed numerical figures — use qualitative thresholds (e.g. \"low LR\", \"small batch\") instead of precise floats like `LR=0.205`.\n\n**Update mechanism.** When execution is unavailable, apply the same validation rules\nand update the conclusions files directly with read/edit/write tools. When execution\nis available, use this helper invocation:\n```bash\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" --write-conclusions \\\n  --conclusions-md \"{{CONCLUSIONS_MD_FILE}}\" \\\n  --conclusions-history-jsonl \"{{CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_FILE}}\" \\\n  --cycle-index {{CYCLE_INDEX}} \\\n  --worker-index {{WORKER_INDEX}} \\\n  --gate-trigger <a|b|c|d> \\\n  --gate-reason \"<one sentence; for (d) name the dimension>\" \\\n  --conclusions-text \"<the full new paragraph>\"\n```\n\n**Pre-flight self-check.** Before invoking the helper, count words (`len(paragraph.split())`) and confirm ≤300, and that the paragraph contains no blank line. Most validation rejections can be avoided here.\n\n**Retry budget — exactly 3 attempts per cycle.** On non-zero exit, read the stderr error, shorten the paragraph (drop the least-decisive sentence, merge two related sentences, or remove qualifiers), and retry. After **3 total attempts** with no success, the update is **discarded** for this cycle: do not retry further, do not write the rejected text anywhere, and append a single memory event with `step=\"conclusions_skip\"` whose `summary` names the last validation error. Underlying findings are not lost — they are already durable in `memory.md`.\n\n**Always log the gate decision.** Inside the regular memory append for the cycle, include `gate=<updated|kept|skipped>; trigger=<a|b|c|d|none>; reason=<one sentence>` in the entry's `summary` or `tags`. Use `skipped` only after the 3-attempt budget is exhausted.\n\n# Example evaluation entry\n```markdown\n### 2026-02-13T16:58:00Z | step=evaluate\n- program: program_3\n- combined_score: 2.54\n- correct: true\n- rubrics: uses_restarts=pass, constraint_optimization=pass, score_threshold=fail\n- evidence: late-stage overlap still visible in stdout trace\n- next_recommendation: raise late-stage overlap penalty and diversify restart seeds\n```\n\n--- MANIFEST ---\n{\n  \"figures\": [\n    {\n      \"attempted_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        6\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 9.0,\n      \"fallback_reason\": \"generate-concept-figure exited non-zero (rc=1)\",\n      \"figure_id\": \"fixed_game_overview\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 10,\n        \"legend\": 9,\n        \"ticks\": 9,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": null,\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 29,\n      \"n_panels\": 1,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 1,\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/fixed_game_overview.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"prompt_log_path\": \"figures/fixed_game_overview.prompts.json\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        2\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        3,\n        3,\n        3,\n        3\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 9.0,\n      \"figure_id\": \"final_reference_comparison\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"scatter\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 10,\n        \"legend\": 9,\n        \"ticks\": 9,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 29,\n      \"n_panels\": 4,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/final_reference_comparison.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/final_reference_comparison.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        3,\n        3,\n        3,\n        3\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n        \"final.metric.reference_fidelity\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        4,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 9.0,\n      \"figure_id\": \"component_comparison\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"scatter\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 10,\n        \"legend\": 9,\n        \"ticks\": 9,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 29,\n      \"n_panels\": 2,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/component_comparison.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/component_comparison.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        2,\n        2\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"result.top_program_01\",\n        \"result.top_program_02\",\n        \"result.top_program_03\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        0,\n        0\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 9.0,\n      \"figure_id\": \"reference_diagnostics\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"scatter\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 10,\n        \"legend\": 9,\n        \"ticks\": 9,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 29,\n      \"n_panels\": 2,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/reference_diagnostics.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/reference_diagnostics.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        3,\n        3\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n--- SOURCE ---\nimport ast\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use('Agg')\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nCOLORS = {'standard': '#c17b14', 'multistart': '#956ba5', 'structure': '#176b8c'}\nCASE_NAMES = {'german_logistic': 'German / logistic', 'german_forest': 'German / forest', 'acs_logistic': 'ACS / logistic', 'acs_forest': 'ACS / forest'}\nplt.rcParams.update({'font.size': 10, 'axes.labelsize': 10, 'axes.titlesize': 10, 'xtick.labelsize': 9, 'ytick.labelsize': 9, 'legend.fontsize': 9, 'pdf.fonttype': 42, 'ps.fonttype': 42, 'axes.spines.top': False, 'axes.spines.right': False})\n\n\ndef provenance(path, inputs):\n    manifest = {'schema_name': 'scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest', 'artifact': {'path': str(path), 'kind': 'figure' if str(path).endswith(('.png', '.pdf')) else 'derived', 'sha256': hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}, 'derived_from': inputs, 'generated_by': {'script_path': 'build_artifacts.py', 'command': ['python', 'build_artifacts.py']}}\n    Path(str(path) + '.prov.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2))\n\n\ndef save_plot(figure, figure_id, inputs):\n    for extension in ('pdf', 'png'):\n        output = Path('figures') / (figure_id + '.' + extension)\n        figure.savefig(output, dpi=300)\n        provenance(output, inputs)\n    plt.close(figure)\n\n\ndef get_caps():\n    tree = ast.parse(Path('source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py').read_text())\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Dict):\n            for key, value in zip(node.keys, node.values):\n                if isinstance(key, ast.Constant) and key.value == 'budgets' and isinstance(value, ast.IfExp):\n                    return ast.literal_eval(value.orelse.orelse), ast.literal_eval(value.orelse.body)\n    raise RuntimeError('No grounded budget configuration')\n\n\ndef selected_cases(episodes):\n    return [(episode['seed'], case) for episode in episodes for case in episode['solution']['cases'] if case['case'] != 'controls' and not case['replay']]\n\n\ndef main():\n    Path('figures').mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    Path('tables').mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    data = json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\n    final_caps, development_caps = get_caps()\n    final_episodes = data['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']\n    final = selected_cases(final_episodes)\n    source = ['@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]']\n    rows = []\n    for seed, case in final:\n        observations = case['observations']\n        cells = np.asarray(case['cells'])\n        repeat_pairs = np.asarray(case['repeat_pairs'])\n        for cap_index, cap in enumerate(final_caps):\n            rows.append({'seed': seed, 'case': case['case'], 'cap': cap, 'structure': cells[cap_index].mean(axis=(0, 1)).tolist(), 'standard': observations['baseline_metrics']['standard'][cap_index], 'multistart': observations['baseline_metrics']['multistart'][cap_index], 'repeat': repeat_pairs[cap_index].mean(axis=(0, 1)).tolist(), 'bootstrap_ci95': observations['fidelity_instance_bootstrap_ci95']})\n    summary = {'final': rows, 'final_caps': final_caps, 'development_caps': development_caps}\n    # @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n    summary['reference_sign_mean'] = float(np.mean([row['structure'][2] for row in rows]))\n    summary['min_reference_sign'] = float(min(row['structure'][2] for row in rows))\n    summary['max_repeat_vector_difference'] = float(max(np.ptp(np.asarray(case['observations']['attributions']), axis=1).max() for seed, case in final))\n    summary['reference_uncertainty'] = {name: float(np.mean([np.mean(case['observations']['reference_uncertainty']) for seed, case in final if case['case'] == name])) for name in CASE_NAMES}\n    figure, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(5.5, 3.85), sharex=True, sharey=True)\n    markers = {'standard': 'o', 'multistart': 's', 'structure': 'D'}\n    labels = {'standard': 'Library one-shot', 'multistart': 'Two-start, split cap', 'structure': 'Structure-aware'}\n    for axis, name in zip(axes.flat, CASE_NAMES):\n        for offset, method in enumerate(labels):\n            means = []\n            for cap_index, cap in enumerate(final_caps):\n                values = [row[method][0] for row in rows if row['case'] == name and row['cap'] == cap]\n                positions = np.full(len(values), cap_index + (offset - 1) * .1)\n                axis.scatter(positions, values, color=COLORS[method], marker=markers[method], alpha=.5, s=13, zorder=4)\n                means.append(np.mean(values))\n            axis.plot(np.arange(len(final_caps)) + (offset - 1) * .1, means, color=COLORS[method], marker=markers[method], markersize=4, label=labels[method], linewidth=1.1)\n        axis.set_title(CASE_NAMES[name] + '\\n' + ('approximate reference' if name.startswith('german') else 'exhaustive reference'), pad=5)\n        axis.set_xticks(range(len(final_caps)), final_caps)\n        axis.set_ylim(0, 1.05)\n        axis.set_yticks([0, .5, 1])\n        axis.grid(axis='y', alpha=.18)\n    for axis in axes[1]:\n        axis.set_xlabel('Coalition cap')\n    for axis in axes[:, 0]:\n        axis.set_ylabel('Reference agreement')\n    handles, legend_labels = axes[0, 0].get_legend_handles_labels()\n    figure.legend(handles, legend_labels, loc='lower center', ncol=3, frameon=False, handlelength=1.1, columnspacing=.7)\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.12, right=.985, top=.88, bottom=.20, hspace=.72, wspace=.22)\n    save_plot(figure, 'final_reference_comparison', source)\n    # @evidence[[paper_data.json#/all_programs]]\n    development = []\n    for config_index, config in enumerate(data['all_programs']):\n        for seed, case in selected_cases(config['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']):\n            for cap_index, cap in enumerate(development_caps):\n                development.append({'configuration': config_index, 'seed': seed, 'case': case['case'], 'cap': cap, 'agreement': float(np.asarray(case['cells'])[cap_index, :, :, 0].mean())})\n    summary['development'] = development\n    figure, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(5.5, 2.65), sharey=True)\n    for axis, kind, before, after in zip(axes, ('forest', 'logistic'), (0, 1), (1, 2)):\n        categories = [(dataset + '_' + kind, cap) for dataset in ('german', 'acs') for cap in development_caps]\n        for config_index, offset, color, label in ((before, -.09, '#9b9b9b', 'Without component'), (after, .09, '#176b8c', 'With component')):\n            for category_index, (name, cap) in enumerate(categories):\n                values = [row['agreement'] for row in development if row['configuration'] == config_index and row['case'] == name and row['cap'] == cap]\n                axis.scatter(np.full(len(values), category_index + offset), values, color=color, s=19, label=label if category_index == 0 else None, zorder=3)\n                axis.plot([category_index + offset - .055, category_index + offset + .055], [np.mean(values)] * 2, color=color, linewidth=2)\n        axis.set_xticks(range(len(categories)), [name.split('_')[0].replace('german', 'Ger').replace('acs', 'ACS') + '\\n' + str(cap) for name, cap in categories])\n        axis.set_title('Exact forest component' if kind == 'forest' else 'Logistic integration component')\n        axis.set_ylim(.80, 1.01)\n        axis.set_yticks([.8, .9, 1.])\n        axis.grid(axis='y', alpha=.18)\n    axes[0].set_ylabel('Reference agreement')\n    figure.legend(*axes[0].get_legend_handles_labels(), loc='lower center', ncol=2, frameon=False)\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.12, right=.985, top=.85, bottom=.28, wspace=.25)\n    save_plot(figure, 'component_comparison', ['@evidence[[paper_data.json#/all_programs]]'])\n    figure, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(5.5, 2.65))\n    for axis, name in zip(axes, ('german_logistic', 'german_forest')):\n        for seed, case in final:\n            if case['case'] != name:\n                continue\n            reference = np.asarray(case['observations']['reference'])\n            estimate = np.asarray(case['observations']['attributions'])[0, 0]\n            half_difference = np.abs(np.asarray(case['observations']['reference_uncertainty'])).sum(axis=-1)\n            observed_distance = np.abs(estimate - reference).sum(axis=-1)\n            axis.scatter(half_difference, observed_distance, alpha=.6, s=12)\n        maximum = max(axis.get_xlim()[1], axis.get_ylim()[1])\n        axis.plot([0, maximum], [0, maximum], color='#777777', linestyle='--', linewidth=.8)\n        axis.set_title(CASE_NAMES[name])\n        axis.set_xlabel('Reference half-difference, L1')\n        axis.set_xlim(left=0)\n        axis.set_ylim(bottom=0)\n        axis.grid(alpha=.15)\n    axes[0].set_ylabel('Estimate-to-reference L1')\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.13, right=.98, bottom=.25, top=.86, wspace=.40)\n    save_plot(figure, 'reference_diagnostics', source)\n    concept = Path('figures/fixed_game_overview.png')\n    log = Path('figures/fixed_game_overview.prompts.json')\n    if not Path('.concept_figure_complete').exists() and not (log.exists() and json.loads(log.read_text())) and not concept.exists():\n        image = Image.new('RGB', (2400, 680), 'white')\n        drawing = ImageDraw.Draw(image)\n        drawing.text((80, 300), 'Conceptual overview reserved for synchronous rendering', fill='#555555')\n        image.save(concept)\n        log.write_text('{}\\n')\n    Path('analysis_summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n    provenance(Path('analysis_summary.json'), source + ['@evidence[[paper_data.json#/all_programs]]'])\n    table_lines = []\n    for name in CASE_NAMES:\n        chosen = [row for row in rows if row['case'] == name and row['cap'] == final_caps[0]]\n        means = {method: np.mean([row[method][0] for row in chosen]) for method in labels}\n        signs = np.mean([row['structure'][2] for row in chosen])\n        table_lines.append(f\"{CASE_NAMES[name]} & {means['standard']:.4f} & {means['multistart']:.4f} & {means['structure']:.4f} & {signs:.4f} \\\\\\\\\")\n    Path('tables/main_rows.tex').write_text('% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n' + '\\n'.join(table_lines) + '\\n')\n    provenance(Path('tables/main_rows.tex'), source)\n    extended = []\n    for row in rows:\n        extended.append(f\"{row['seed']} & {CASE_NAMES[row['case']]} & {row['cap']} & {row['standard'][0]:.4f} & {row['multistart'][0]:.4f} & {row['structure'][0]:.4f} \\\\\\\\\")\n    Path('tables/extended_rows.tex').write_text('% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n' + '\\n'.join(extended) + '\\n')\n    provenance(Path('tables/extended_rows.tex'), source)\n    intervals = []\n    for seed, case in final:\n        interval = case['observations']['fidelity_instance_bootstrap_ci95']\n        intervals.append(f\"{seed} & {CASE_NAMES[case['case']]} & [{interval[0]:.10f}, {interval[1]:.10f}] \\\\\\\\\")\n    Path('tables/interval_rows.tex').write_text('% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n' + '\\n'.join(intervals) + '\\n')\n    provenance(Path('tables/interval_rows.tex'), source)\n    specs = json.loads(Path('paper_strategy.json').read_text())['figure_specs']\n    figures = []\n    for spec in specs:\n        figure_id = spec['figure_id']\n        concept_figure = spec['preferred_generator'] == 'generate-concept-figure'\n        entry = {'figure_id': figure_id, 'figure_type': spec['figure_type'], 'generator': spec['preferred_generator'], 'path_png': 'figures/' + figure_id + '.png', 'n_panels': spec['max_panels'], 'n_rows': 2 if figure_id == 'final_reference_comparison' else 1, 'n_cols': 2 if spec['max_panels'] > 1 else 1, 'source_ids': spec['source_ids'], 'categories_per_panel': [spec['max_categories_per_panel']] * spec['max_panels'], 'series_per_panel': [spec['max_series_per_panel']] * spec['max_panels'], 'font_sizes': {'title': 10, 'axis': 10, 'ticks': 9, 'legend': 9}, 'placement': 'full_width', 'intended_latex_width_fraction': 1.0, 'estimated_min_rendered_font_pt': 9.0}\n        if concept_figure:\n            entry['prompt_log_path'] = 'figures/' + figure_id + '.prompts.json'\n        else:\n            entry['path_pdf'] = 'figures/' + figure_id + '.pdf'\n        figures.append(entry)\n    figures.append({'figure_id': 'reference_diagnostics', 'figure_type': 'scatter', 'generator': 'matplotlib', 'path_pdf': 'figures/reference_diagnostics.pdf', 'path_png': 'figures/reference_diagnostics.png', 'n_panels': 2, 'n_rows': 1, 'n_cols': 2, 'categories_per_panel': [0, 0], 'series_per_panel': [3, 3], 'source_ids': ['final.evidence.episodes'], 'font_sizes': {'title': 10, 'axis': 10, 'ticks': 9, 'legend': 9}, 'placement': 'full_width', 'intended_latex_width_fraction': 1.0, 'estimated_min_rendered_font_pt': 9.0})\n    for entry in figures:\n        entry['panels_per_row'] = entry.pop('n_cols')\n        entry.pop('n_rows')\n        entry['max_label_chars'] = 29\n        entry['uses_abbrev_labels'] = True\n        entry['uses_progression'] = False\n        if entry['figure_type'] in ('grouped_dot', 'paired_dot'):\n            entry['figure_type'] = 'scatter'\n    Path('figure_manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'figures': figures}, indent=2))\n    print('Final reference sign mean:', summary['reference_sign_mean'])\n    print('Reference uncertainty:', summary['reference_uncertainty'])\n    print('Repeat vector max difference:', summary['max_repeat_vector_difference'])\n    for name in CASE_NAMES:\n        print(name, [[round(np.mean([row[method][0] for row in rows if row['case'] == name and row['cap'] == cap]), 6) for cap in final_caps] for method in labels])\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n\n--- LATEX FIGURES ---\n1:\\documentclass{article}\n20:\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,graphicx,booktabs,subcaption,longtable}\n47:\\begin{figure}[t]\n49:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/fixed_game_overview.png}\n50:\\caption{Computational reliability for a fixed explanation game. Sampled and structure-aware calculations target the same finite-background probability game. Repeat consistency and reference agreement answer different questions; neither establishes deployment validity.}\n177:\\begin{figure}[t]\n179:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/final_reference_comparison.pdf}\n180:\\caption{Final reference agreement by dataset, classifier, and coalition cap. Dots show the three fitted-condition seeds; lines connect cap-wise means, not a temporal trajectory. German references average two high-cap estimates; ACS references are exhaustive. The common zero-to-one scale makes the severe split-cap German failure visible; Table~\\ref{tab:main} resolves near-ceiling differences.}\n187:\\caption{Final cap-64 mean reference agreement and structure-aware reference sign agreement, averaged over seeds. The top-three reference overlap is 1 throughout for the structure-aware computation. Values rounded to 1.0000 are not claims of exact real-arithmetic equality.}\n233:\\begin{figure}[t]\n235:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/component_comparison.pdf}\n236:\\caption{Matched component comparisons on development data only. Left: forest computation with and without the exact leaf-game component. Right: logistic computation with and without integration. Each category shows the two recorded seed values and a mean tick; the vertical axis is restricted to $[0.8,1]$. Ger/ACS denote dataset and labels underneath give coalition caps. The unchanged model family is retained in each comparison; structural access and work still differ.}\n266:\\bibliography{references}\n267:\\bibliographystyle{paper}\n269:\\appendix\n326:\\caption{Final seed/condition/cap reference agreement. Display precision can hide residual error near one.}\\label{tab:extended}\\\\\n373:\\caption{Stored 95\\% instance-bootstrap intervals for structure-aware reference agreement, conditional on each fitted model and reference. ACS values rounding to one have residuals below the displayed resolution.}\n396:\\begin{figure}[t]\n398:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/reference_diagnostics.pdf}\n399:\\caption{German reference diagnostics. Each dot is a retained query/seed pair; color distinguishes seeds. The horizontal coordinate is the L1 norm of the two reference estimates' coordinatewise half-difference. The vertical coordinate is structure-aware distance to their mean at the smallest cap and first repeat. The dashed line marks equality of these descriptive distances, not a calibrated uncertainty boundary.}\n\n--- LOCAL RULES ---\n\n--- STATUS ---\nfatal: not a git repository (or any parent up to mount point /)\nStopping at filesystem boundary (GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM not set).\n","exit_code":128,"status":"failed"}}
