{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"ls /workspace/task/.venv/bin | head -25; sed -n '1,100p' .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md; rg -n 'PNG width|PNG height|estimated_min_rendered|font_sizes|placement' /workspace/task/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/src/orchestrator/paper_step.py | head -30; printf '\\\\n--- RECORD MEMORY ---\\\\n'; python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --global-memory-md ./global_memory/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl ./global_memory/memory.jsonl --event-json '{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Targeted figure repair: no hard errors; three source-generated plots have undersized PNGs. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Figure export changes do not alter scientific conclusions.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Feedback lists three 1650px plot widths and one 680px concept height; quantitative LaTeX references already use PDFs. Overview asset is a placeholder with failed generation, not a recoverable conceptual diagram source.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Regenerate quantitative PDF/PNG exports with proportionally scaled typography at 300 DPI and at least 2400px width; retain and disclose unresolved conceptual placeholder warning; rerun canonical validators.\\\"}'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"ls /workspace/task/.venv/bin | head -25; sed -n '1,100p' .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md; rg -n 'PNG width|PNG height|estimated_min_rendered|font_sizes|placement' /workspace/task/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/src/orchestrator/paper_step.py | head -30; printf '\\\\n--- RECORD MEMORY ---\\\\n'; python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --global-memory-md ./global_memory/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl ./global_memory/memory.jsonl --event-json '{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Targeted figure repair: no hard errors; three source-generated plots have undersized PNGs. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Figure export changes do not alter scientific conclusions.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Feedback lists three 1650px plot widths and one 680px concept height; quantitative LaTeX references already use PDFs. Overview asset is a placeholder with failed generation, not a recoverable conceptual diagram source.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Regenerate quantitative PDF/PNG exports with proportionally scaled typography at 300 DPI and at least 2400px width; retain and disclose unresolved conceptual placeholder warning; rerun canonical validators.\\\"}'\"","aggregated_output":"Activate.ps1\nactivate\nactivate.csh\nactivate.fish\nagsci\nf2py\nidna\nnormalizer\nnumba\nnumpy-config\npip\npip3\npip3.12\npython\npython3\npython3.12\ntqdm\nwheel\n---\nname: scientific-evidence\ndescription: |\n  Use when: you start writing a scientific paper.\n  Outputs: a repo-local `scientific-evidence/` bundle generated by the skill script, plus the conventions, schemas, and verification report needed for downstream evidence tracking and auditing.\n---\n\n# scientific-evidence\n\nUse this skill to define or materialize a generic evidence contract for scientific artifacts.\n\nAlways use this skill during paper writing whenever the agent adds quantitative content: manuscript numbers, table entries, figure inputs, derived statistics, or plotting/calculation scripts.\n\n## What this skill is for\n\nThe point of this skill is simple: an agent should not be able to drop important numbers, figures, or derived outputs into a paper without leaving a machine-checkable trail back to real artifacts.\n\nThis skill gives the agent one fixed place and one fixed grammar for that trail:\n- inline `@evidence[[...]]` refs in text-like files\n- `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts\n- a central `scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl` for optional structured rollups\n\nIt is deliberately generic. The base contract works even when the workflow spans Python, bash, LaTeX, Markdown, JSON, logs, or other file formats.\n\n## Default workflow\n\n1. Read the current paper/results layout, but do not invent a new evidence layout.\n2. Use the fixed directory structure rooted at `scientific-evidence/`.\n3. Run the skill script first instead of inventing schemas by hand:\n```bash\nbash src/agents/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh --help\nbash src/agents/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh emit-bundle --root-dir <workspace-root>\n```\n4. For every quantitative paper-writing action, use this skill contract:\n- adding a number to `paper.tex`\n- filling a table cell\n- writing a plotting script\n- writing a calculation/statistics script\n- generating a figure, table, or derived JSON file\n5. Inside plotting or calculation scripts, do not hardcode experiment numbers that should come from artifacts. Read them from files, then leave the corresponding `@evidence[[...]]` refs near the read/derivation logic.\n6. Add inline evidence refs in text-like artifacts and `.prov.json` sidecars for generated outputs.\n7. Run the verifier after the agent writes claims, scripts, figures, or sidecars:\n```bash\nbash src/agents/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh verify --root-dir <workspace-root>\n```\n8. Inspect `scientific-evidence/verification-report.json` and fail hard on dangling links.\n9. Treat the generated markdown spec and JSON Schemas as canonical for downstream agents.\nKeep the verifier behavior explicit:\n- `resolved`: target artifact exists and the verifier can check the locator semantics it understands.\n- `anchored`: target artifact exists, but the locator stays opaque or only hash/path checks were possible.\n- `dangling`: the target or manifest link does not resolve.\n\n## How this is used to verify agent work\n\nVerification works by checking whether the agent left a connected evidence trail.\n\nAt a minimum, a downstream verifier should be able to:\n- scan manuscript text, scripts, and notes for `@evidence[[...]]` refs\n- read `.prov.json` sidecars for figures, tables, and other generated outputs\n- resolve those refs against real files or stable ids\n- classify each link as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`\n- fail when a generated artifact has no input trail or when a claimed source does not exist\n\nThis does not prove every scientific claim automatically. It does prove whether the agent left enough structure for an auditor or stricter verifier to replay and inspect the work instead of trusting free-form prose.\n\nA core policy for paper writing is: do not hardcode result numbers inside plotting or calculation scripts when those values should be read from real artifacts. Read from files, derive from those inputs, and attach `@evidence[[...]]` refs that point back to the inputs.\n\n## Fixed directory structure\n\n```text\nscientific-evidence/\n  spec.md\n  bundle.manifest.json\n  ledger.jsonl\n  schemas/\n    evidence-reference.schema.json\n    artifact-manifest.schema.json\n    ledger-entry.schema.json\n    verification-report.schema.json\n```\n\n## Grammar summary\n\n- Evidence ref token: `@evidence[[TARGET]]` or `@evidence[[TARGET#LOCATOR]]`\n- `TARGET` may be a relative path, absolute path, URI, or stable identifier.\n- `LOCATOR` is opaque unless a verifier adapter knows how to interpret it.\n- Generated artifact sidecar name: `<artifact>.prov.json`\n- Central ledger file: `scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl`\n\n## Schema set\n\nGenerate the canonical schema bundle with the script. The bundle includes:\n- `scientific-evidence/spec.md`\n- `scientific-evidence/schemas/evidence-reference.schema.json`\n- `scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json`\n- `scientific-evidence/schemas/ledger-entry.schema.json`\n- `scientific-evidence/schemas/verification-report.schema.json`\n- `scientific-evidence/bundle.manifest.json`\n- `scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl`\n\n797:    \"\"\"Read top-level image placements without recursing into Form XObjects.\"\"\"\n1326:    \"\"\"Read PNG width and height from the IHDR chunk.\"\"\"\n1483:    placement = payload.get(\"placement\")\n1484:    if placement is not None and placement not in {\"half-width\", \"full-width\"}:\n3072:      * ``preferred_span``   -> ``--placement {full-width|half-width}``\n3115:        placement = \"full-width\" if span == \"full_width\" else \"half-width\"\n3121:            \"placement\": placement,\n3136:        re.compile(r\"^figures\\[\\d+\\]\\.font_sizes\\.\"),\n3139:        re.compile(r\"^figures\\[\\d+\\] PNG width too small:\"),\n3140:        re.compile(r\"^figures\\[\\d+\\] PNG height too small:\"),\n3157:    \"PNG width too small\",\n3158:    \"PNG height too small\",\n3459:        if row.font_sizes is not None:\n3461:                font_value = row.font_sizes.get(key)\n3463:                    errors.append(f\"figures[{idx}].font_sizes.{key} missing\")\n3466:                        f\"figures[{idx}].font_sizes.{key} below minimum: {font_value} < {minimum}\"\n3479:            if row.placement == \"full_width\":\n3481:            elif row.placement == \"column\":\n3487:                errors.append(f\"figures[{idx}] PNG width too small: {width} < {min_width}\")\n3489:                errors.append(f\"figures[{idx}] PNG height too small: {height} < {min_height}\")\n\n--- RECORD MEMORY ---\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\", line 419, in <module>\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n                     ^^^^^^\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\", line 415, in main\n    return _run_append_event(args)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\", line 405, in _run_append_event\n    _append_text(global_memory_md_path, _markdown_entry(event), header=GLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER)\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\", line 126, in _append_text\n    fd = _open_regular_for_append(path)\n         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\", line 161, in _open_regular_for_append\n    directory_fd = _walk_directory_no_follow(path.parent)\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/workspace/paper/.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\", line 198, in _walk_directory_no_follow\n    next_descriptor = os.open(component, flags, dir_fd=descriptor)\n                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nNotADirectoryError: [Errno 20] Not a directory: 'global_memory'\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
