{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' /workspace/task/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/src/orchestrator/paper_venues.py; sed -n '1,35p' paper.tex; rg -n 'PAGE_LIMITS|def detect_paper_format' /workspace/task/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/src/orchestrator/paper_step.py; rg --files /workspace/task | rg '(venues.*json|iclr.*json|venue.*catalog)' | head -10; tail -10 paper.log; ls -1 /usr/bin | rg 'pdf|mutool|xpdf'\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Catalog of paper venues declared under ``configs/venue/<name>.yaml``.\n\nA venue bundles everything the paper stages need to know about one paper\nformat: the writer brief, the canonical author block, the LaTeX template\ndirectory, the markers that identify a compiled manuscript, the enforced page\nbudget, and the venue-specific checks it opts into. Adding a venue is adding a\nYAML file plus the referenced brief and template files; no Python changes.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport yaml\n\nREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent\nVENUE_DIR = REPO_ROOT / \"configs\" / \"venue\"\nVENUE_NAME_RE = re.compile(r\"^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}$\")\n\n#: Behavioural checks implemented in ``paper_step``; a venue opts in by name.\nKNOWN_CHECKS = frozenset({\"alife_framing\"})\n_SPEC_KEYS = frozenset(\n    {\n        \"name\",\n        \"brief\",\n        \"author_block\",\n        \"template_dir\",\n        \"latex_markers\",\n        \"page_budget\",\n        \"checks\",\n    }\n)\n_PAGE_BUDGET_KEYS = frozenset(\n    {\n        \"min_body_pages\",\n        \"max_body_pages\",\n        \"min_last_body_page_fill_ratio\",\n        \"body_columns\",\n        \"exclude_references\",\n    }\n)\n\n\nclass VenueSpecError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"A venue file is missing, malformed, or references missing assets.\"\"\"\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass PageBudget:\n    \"\"\"Page budget enforced by ``validate_page_budget``.\"\"\"\n\n    max_body_pages: int\n    min_body_pages: int | None = None\n    min_last_body_page_fill_ratio: float | None = None\n    body_columns: int = 1\n    exclude_references: bool = False\n\n    def as_limits(self) -> dict[str, int | float | bool]:\n        \"\"\"Return the mapping shape ``validate_page_budget`` consumes.\"\"\"\n        limits: dict[str, int | float | bool] = {\n            \"max_body_pages\": self.max_body_pages,\n            \"body_columns\": self.body_columns,\n            \"exclude_references\": self.exclude_references,\n        }\n        if self.min_body_pages is not None:\n            limits[\"min_body_pages\"] = self.min_body_pages\n        if self.min_last_body_page_fill_ratio is not None:\n            limits[\"min_last_body_page_fill_ratio\"] = self.min_last_body_page_fill_ratio\n        return limits\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass VenueSpec:\n    \"\"\"One paper venue as declared in ``configs/venue/<name>.yaml``.\"\"\"\n\n    name: str\n    brief: str\n    author_block: str | None\n    template_dir: str\n    latex_markers: tuple[str, ...]\n    page_budget: PageBudget | None\n    checks: frozenset[str]\n\n    @property\n    def brief_path(self) -> Path:\n        return REPO_ROOT / self.brief\n\n    @property\n    def author_block_path(self) -> Path | None:\n        return REPO_ROOT / self.author_block if self.author_block is not None else None\n\n    def matches_tex(self, tex_text: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Report whether *tex_text* carries one of this venue's LaTeX markers.\"\"\"\n        return any(re.search(marker, tex_text, re.IGNORECASE) for marker in self.latex_markers)\n\n\n\\documentclass{article}\n% --- watermark (auto-inserted) ---\n\\usepackage{xcolor}\n\\usepackage{xfp}% \\fpeval; in the kernel since 2022, harmless on older LaTeX\n\\usepackage{draftwatermark}\n\\newlength{\\watermarkTextWidth}\n\\AddToHook{begindocument/end}{%\n  \\SetWatermarkText{\\normalfont Generated by The Agentic Scientist}%\n  \\SetWatermarkFontSize{10pt}%\n  \\SetWatermarkLightness{0.85}%\n  \\settowidth{\\watermarkTextWidth}{\\normalfont\\fontsize{10pt}{12pt}\\selectfont Generated by The Agentic Scientist}%\n  \\edef\\watermarkScale{\\fpeval{0.8 * sqrt(\\paperwidth**2 + \\paperheight**2) / \\watermarkTextWidth}}%\n  \\edef\\watermarkAngle{\\fpeval{atand(\\paperheight/\\paperwidth)}}%\n  \\SetWatermarkScale{\\watermarkScale}%\n  \\SetWatermarkAngle{\\watermarkAngle}%\n}\n% --- end watermark ---\n\n\\usepackage{paper,times}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,graphicx,booktabs,subcaption,longtable}\n\\usepackage{hyperref,url}\n\\title{Fixed-Game SHAP Reliability:\\\\Structure, Budgets, and Reference Limits}\n\\author{}\n\\newcommand{\\norm}[1]{\\left\\lVert #1\\right\\rVert_1}\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nA feature attribution can be repeatable without accurately computing its intended explanation, and accurate without justifying a decision. We isolate the computational question for frozen tabular classifiers: agreement with a fixed empirical, probability-scale Shapley game under finite coalition caps. We compare library Kernel SHAP, averaging two split-cap estimates, and structure-aware computation using forest leaf constraints and logistic integration. German Credit and an explicitly adapted ACS income task provide logistic and forest conditions with different reference quality. Across the retained final evaluation, structure-aware outputs have mean normalized reference agreement of 0.99756 and identical observed attribution vectors across repeated calls; their top-three sets agree with every reference. However, German references are approximate, and the structure-aware methods access model parameters rather than spending the same prediction-only budget. Split-cap averaging is particularly weak at the smallest German cap. These results support a narrow computational-reliability claim for the evaluated fixed games, not equal-time superiority, robustness to background changes, or reliable reasons for high-stakes decisions.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/reference_fidelity]]\n% @evidence[[analysis_summary.json#/max_repeat_vector_difference]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Introduction}\n275:PAGE_LIMITS: dict[str, dict[str, int | float | bool]] = page_limits()\n649:def detect_paper_format(tex_text: str) -> str | None:\n1203:    budget = PAGE_LIMITS.get(paper_format) if paper_format is not None else None\n/share/texlive/texmf-dist/fonts/type1/urw/times/utmb8a.pfb></usr/share/texlive/\ntexmf-dist/fonts/type1/urw/times/utmr8a.pfb></usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/font\ns/type1/urw/times/utmri8a.pfb>\nOutput written on paper.pdf (15 pages, 299296 bytes).\nPDF statistics:\n 495 PDF objects out of 1000 (max. 8388607)\n 357 compressed objects within 4 object streams\n 97 named destinations out of 1000 (max. 500000)\n 181 words of extra memory for PDF output out of 10000 (max. 10000000)\n\ndvipdfm\ndvipdfmx\ndvipdft\nepspdf\nepspdftk\nmptopdf\npdfannotextractor\npdfatfi\npdfclose\npdfetex\npdflatex\npdflatex-dev\npdfopen\npdftex\npdftosrc\npn2pdf\nsimpdftex\nthumbpdf\ntpic2pdftex\nxdvipdfmx\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
